    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-6166",
      "problem": "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $1$st, $3$rd and $4$th rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14241016/assets/0762a271e9caae7f2b2ac4e03590753cd2e49bef78dc4cf769565fa01ec4c9e7.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $1$st, $3$rd and $4$th rows of $A$ are $-1$, $-4$ and $8$, respectively.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14241016/assets/c2c52023255e70131f4c8cf205b5ee1856996d6dab7d055c405bbb522cb6c09b.svg)\n\nSo, the answer is $-1+(-4)+8=3.$",
